new_candidates.body:
Bug report

- Operating system: Ubuntu 22.04
- Installation type: binaries
- Version: Humble, rclcpp 16.0.8 (code unchanged in 16.0.21)
- DDS implementation: Fast DDS (`rmw_fastrtps_cpp`)
- Client library: rclcpp

#### Steps to reproduce
A composable node that keeps one extra callback group alive as a member (added to the executor automatically) with a timer on it:

```cpp
#include <chrono>
#include <rclcpp/rclcpp.hpp>
#include <rclcpp_components/register_node_macro.hpp>

namespace repro
{
// Parameter extra_group:=false puts the timer on the default group (the control case).
class TwoGroup : public rclcpp::Node
{
public:
  explicit TwoGroup(const rclcpp::NodeOptions & options)
  : Node("two_group", options)
  {
    if (declare_parameter("extra_group", true)) {
      group_ = create_callback_group(rclcpp::CallbackGroupType::MutuallyExclusive);
    }
    timer_ = create_wall_timer(std::chrono::seconds(1), [] {}, group_);
  }

private:
  rclcpp::CallbackGroup::SharedPtr group_;
  rclcpp::TimerBase::SharedPtr timer_;
};
}  // namespace repro

RCLCPP_COMPONENTS_REGISTER_NODE(repro::TwoGroup)
```

CMake: `add_library(two_group SHARED ...)` plus `rclcpp_components_register_nodes(two_group "repro::TwoGroup")`.

```bash
/opt/ros/humble/lib/rclcpp_components/component_container_mt --ros-args -r __node:=repro_container &
ros2 component load /repro_container two_group_repro repro::TwoGroup -p extra_group:=true
ros2 component unload /repro_container 1
```

#### Expected behaviour
The node unloads and the container keeps running.

#### Actual behaviour
- `component_container_mt`: segmentation fault right after the unload (3/3 runs). With `extra_group:=false` (timer on the default group) the container survives (3/3).
- `component_container` (single-threaded): aborts (SIGABRT) with `extra_group:=true`; survives with `false`.
- In a larger node, gdb shows the fault in `__rmw_wait` (rmw_fastrtps_shared_cpp) on the guard condition of one of the removed node's callback groups, already destroyed by `~NodeBase`.

#### Additional information
`Executor::remove_node` calls `remove_callback_group_from_map` for each of the node's groups. That function removes the group's guard condition from the memory strategy, and erases it from `weak_groups_to_guard_conditions_`, only inside the `!has_node(...) && !has_node(...)` branch, which is true only for the node's last group. Every earlier group's guard condition stays in the memory strategy as a raw pointer and dangles once the node is destroyed. The expired-group cleanup in `wait_for_work` does not catch it, because `remove_callback_group_from_map` has already erased the group from `weak_groups_to_nodes_`. Jazzy's executor rewrite removed this code; a Humble fix would move the guard-condition removal out of that branch.
